From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:42:30 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 52/58] Input: melfas_mip4 - do not loop on a zero event size

The interrupt handler walks the packet in steps of the event size the
controller reported at probe time. If the controller reports a size of 0
(or the query failed), the loop never advances and the threaded handler
spins until the soft lockup detector fires, as seen with Samsung MSS100
firmware. Drop such packets instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I80154e5350b32f868e235f75ad3004ad48d84a72
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
index 94f8ad13f..b9502d1ca 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
@@ -640,6 +640,9 @@ static irqreturn_t mip4_interrupt(int irq, void *dev_id)
 
 	if (alert) {
 		dev_dbg(&client->dev, "Alert: %d\n", ts->buf[0]);
+	} else if (!ts->event_size) {
+		dev_err_ratelimited(&client->dev,
+				    "Unknown event size, packet dropped\n");
 	} else {
 		for (i = 0; i < size; i += ts->event_size) {
 			error = mip4_handle_packet(ts, &ts->buf[i]);
